{'base__uid': 1363, 'base__ref_base': 'G', 'base__alt_base': 'T', 'base__hugo': 'TNFRSF18', 'base__cchange': 'c.310+315C>A', 'base__so': 'INT', 'clinvar__disease_names': None, 'clinvar__id': None, 'dbsnp__rsid': 'rs1815606', 'gnomad__af': 0.509314384482, 'omim__omim_id': None, 'vcfinfo__zygosity': 'het', 'ncbigene__ncbi_desc': 'This gene encodes a member of the TNF-receptor superfamily. The encoded receptor has been shown to have increased expression upon T-cell activation, and it is thought to play a key role in dominant immunological self-tolerance maintained by CD25(+)CD4(+) regulatory T cells. Knockout studies in mice also suggest the role of this receptor is in the regulation of CD3-driven T-cell activation and programmed cell death. Three alternatively spliced transcript variants of this gene encoding distinct isoforms have been reported. [provided by RefSeq, Feb 2011]'}
{'base__uid': 1364, 'base__ref_base': 'G', 'base__alt_base': 'A', 'base__hugo': 'TNFRSF18', 'base__cchange': 'c.-308C>T', 'base__so': '2KU', 'clinvar__disease_names': None, 'clinvar__id': None, 'dbsnp__rsid': 'rs185269291', 'gnomad__af': 0.00133902952241, 'omim__omim_id': None, 'vcfinfo__zygosity': 'het', 'ncbigene__ncbi_desc': 'This gene encodes a member of the TNF-receptor superfamily. The encoded receptor has been shown to have increased expression upon T-cell activation, and it is thought to play a key role in dominant immunological self-tolerance maintained by CD25(+)CD4(+) regulatory T cells. Knockout studies in mice also suggest the role of this receptor is in the regulation of CD3-driven T-cell activation and programmed cell death. Three alternatively spliced transcript variants of this gene encoding distinct isoforms have been reported. [provided by RefSeq, Feb 2011]'}
{'base__uid': 1365, 'base__ref_base': 'C', 'base__alt_base': 'T', 'base__hugo': 'TNFRSF4', 'base__cchange': 'c.534G>A', 'base__so': 'SYN', 'clinvar__disease_names': 'Combined immunodeficiency due to OX40 deficiency|not specified|not provided', 'clinvar__id': '403556', 'dbsnp__rsid': 'rs17568', 'gnomad__af': 0.359815397158, 'omim__omim_id': None, 'vcfinfo__zygosity': 'het', 'ncbigene__ncbi_desc': 'The protein encoded by this gene is a member of the TNF-receptor superfamily. This receptor has been shown to activate NF-kappaB through its interaction with adaptor proteins TRAF2 and TRAF5. Knockout studies in mice suggested that this receptor promotes the expression of apoptosis inhibitors BCL2 and BCL2lL1/BCL2-XL, and thus suppresses apoptosis. The knockout studies also suggested the roles of this receptor in CD4+ T cell response, as well as in T cell-dependent B cell proliferation and differentiation. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008]'}
