{'base__uid': 2273, 'base__ref_base': 'C', 'base__alt_base': 'A', 'base__hugo': 'GNB1', 'base__cchange': 'c.*3491G>T', 'base__so': '2KD', 'clinvar__disease_names': None, 'clinvar__id': None, 'dbsnp__rsid': 'rs742359', 'gnomad__af': 0.239971850809, 'omim__omim_id': None, 'vcfinfo__zygosity': 'het', 'ncbigene__ncbi_desc': 'Heterotrimeric guanine nucleotide-binding proteins (G proteins), which integrate signals between receptors and effector proteins, are composed of an alpha, a beta, and a gamma subunit. These subunits are encoded by families of related genes. This gene encodes a beta subunit. Beta subunits are important regulators of alpha subunits, as well as of certain signal transduction receptors and effectors. Alternative splicing results in multiple transcript variants. [provided by RefSeq, Sep 2013]'}
